[{:db/id "q-82912/selection/faad0727b2c62b6cced88abf9b210ea8763c2fd1c03c01c27346d66484992037" :answer/id #uuid "3238acd5-37f9-5d6e-9fe6-72f2c0e8c825" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82912/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "f6021ad0-530d-5bea-b8ab-492e6b5d46bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82912/selection/9f6bfd6fa85d96298a99db901d9b73f609ef64ac0bcf5fbdc4a7ac6d3b733558" :answer/id #uuid "0a43d897-4648-5104-a08f-630c5bd82d0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82912/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "435cc04a-0e20-5543-b697-bab4ca218714" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82912/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" :answer/id #uuid "860c2c98-1473-5976-944c-b03de3aca131" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82912/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0f6762de-bb82-50a8-9ef8-94b7cca9dd5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-82912/selection/9f6bfd6fa85d96298a99db901d9b73f609ef64ac0bcf5fbdc4a7ac6d3b733558" :answer-field/choices ["q-82912/selection/faad0727b2c62b6cced88abf9b210ea8763c2fd1c03c01c27346d66484992037" "q-82912/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" "q-82912/selection/9f6bfd6fa85d96298a99db901d9b73f609ef64ac0bcf5fbdc4a7ac6d3b733558" "q-82912/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-82912/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-82912" :question/id #uuid "a83a268b-4ca6-5beb-99fc-956e59fdabb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-82912" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ given that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{2\\cdot 0+3\\cdot 1+(-5)\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 2}{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{(-1)}^{2}+{2}^{2}}{a}_{1}=2[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{2\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 1+(-5)\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot (-1)}{{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\overset{^}{x}) & =‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2-3)^{2}+(3-3)^{2}+(-5-(-3))^{2}+(2-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-82912/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8eb07a32-45bd-5975-9f61-de6294d4895d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82912"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-82952/selection/56ad0e0cbf66fa6af852764df04b45752196855270b5e36e53bfa957c3aa5722" :answer/id #uuid "f12df48f-8f42-5a91-8986-8bfed328c137" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{49.11}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82952/selection/3b8df88ef03460f84a0b7e5e97adde1afc8ba7547a5303de968b0f7c21837b5c" :answer/id #uuid "d3a97856-161b-5d66-a844-2612a84fb2a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{40.20}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82952/selection/7e572ec84582d0253f36f4d8f637dbfb028285d74740717117a25db3c6aae847" :answer/id #uuid "0850cc70-58a2-5c21-9a64-de3ae376772d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{23.58}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82952/selection/291f855b0d1996d4eaf3a953c9e1ce7d997a979c9100f669a1639da169feb282" :answer/id #uuid "8675bade-c9b3-540c-8993-c449bab62fe0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{56.22}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82952/selection/ad663b72a59b7e6ce91238675d0f68c435617ec55df8213bf1013cb78bcc8352" :answer/id #uuid "56ebd5e9-809f-51c9-aa09-071080265ca8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{37.33}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82952/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "39a0d3e0-d366-5154-9582-ba12b2b89791" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-82952/selection/56ad0e0cbf66fa6af852764df04b45752196855270b5e36e53bfa957c3aa5722" :answer-field/choices ["q-82952/selection/56ad0e0cbf66fa6af852764df04b45752196855270b5e36e53bfa957c3aa5722" "q-82952/selection/3b8df88ef03460f84a0b7e5e97adde1afc8ba7547a5303de968b0f7c21837b5c" "q-82952/selection/7e572ec84582d0253f36f4d8f637dbfb028285d74740717117a25db3c6aae847" "q-82952/selection/291f855b0d1996d4eaf3a953c9e1ce7d997a979c9100f669a1639da169feb282" "q-82952/selection/ad663b72a59b7e6ce91238675d0f68c435617ec55df8213bf1013cb78bcc8352"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-82952" :question/id #uuid "8b05316e-d9ed-54ce-819d-249152d92fa4" :question/math-academy-id "q-82952" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the acute angle between $x$ and the subspace $S$ given that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{5\\cdot 3+5\\cdot 0+2\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 1}{{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{5\\cdot 2+5\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2+3\\cdot (-2)}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x$ or any other non-zero vector that is parallel to ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ \n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{x\\cdot {\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x}{‖x‖\\,‖{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 5+5\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0+3\\cdot (-1)}{\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{5}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{\\sqrt{63}\\sqrt{27}} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{3\\sqrt{7}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{7})≈{49.11}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-82952/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c93bf305-85ff-5455-91ba-ae60f3c1989d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82952"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-82955/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer/id #uuid "da4877d0-6c64-5db2-8dc9-20a8d3671d6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82955/selection/d62732e72e17b0393290bd9e548ef368f6b7424bded817d038b07db5bf5fcb98" :answer/id #uuid "569a6418-36db-5075-bdcd-e903d55c84e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82955/selection/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" :answer/id #uuid "e73c28d1-cf41-581b-884a-798ad9791a58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82955/selection/e0bd991ac2e2f2a23ec920e03c6d5103be6b20c12a25d724ab290d4ba5292c3e" :answer/id #uuid "1470f1f9-cc0a-5bac-a188-05d5e8e0954d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82955/selection/33a41d785f2131b936fe2f759b0ab5fbc693f77aac923ea2f44f0b0960b4fb32" :answer/id #uuid "27069e9f-a030-5063-9b64-a55bb650815f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82955/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b27e762f-9c03-5e9f-ab7d-9a2d27ca4305" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-82955/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer-field/choices ["q-82955/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" "q-82955/selection/d62732e72e17b0393290bd9e548ef368f6b7424bded817d038b07db5bf5fcb98" "q-82955/selection/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" "q-82955/selection/e0bd991ac2e2f2a23ec920e03c6d5103be6b20c12a25d724ab290d4ba5292c3e" "q-82955/selection/33a41d785f2131b936fe2f759b0ab5fbc693f77aac923ea2f44f0b0960b4fb32"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-82955" :question/id #uuid "b54810db-204b-54de-896d-8657b81a4f59" :question/math-academy-id "q-82955" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the acute angle between $x$ and the subspace $S$ given that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{3\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{3}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{3\\cdot 2+4\\cdot (-1)+(-3)\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 1}{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x$ or any other non-zero vector that is parallel to ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ So, to make calculations easier, we can find the angle between the vectors\n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,2\\,{\\text{proj}}_{S}x=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 7+4\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 5}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{7}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{5}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{38}{\\sqrt{38}\\sqrt{76}} \\\\  & =\\frac{38}{38\\cdot \\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{4},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-82955/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c93bf305-85ff-5455-91ba-ae60f3c1989d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82955"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140363/selection/eba8ed19051b1c86febb753ff1f361fda7d042ce44e03ec8c3d9a6ee23164c50" :answer/id #uuid "055f97e4-6816-5c37-bc46-83691b86f1aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140363/selection/415411ac4222f8d7004483a8d45b8894eb258ef4b817965128ee936d1f6dc577" :answer/id #uuid "a0df0db0-5196-5162-affa-2a7891657598" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140363/selection/13a2c3dec80713ec93b0c7add6e42720c6ac44313e2be81191f977bd4ee58dfd" :answer/id #uuid "58fe3b20-37cc-5459-8e68-e0f8bada6c7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140363/selection/0fd1f53d810123760f0a4dea5516a22798ac28fdc9ee9b8aac95b13bef853fb1" :answer/id #uuid "c6af211d-3e87-53dd-b488-022c6dffb945" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140363/selection/de81b9d7ecf817e60cb92e53a68b955801e63a5b48151989590729efe8d4345c" :answer/id #uuid "91332da9-8eb3-52d6-b0ba-d483aef5752b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140363/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ad82d57-2701-59ec-99a6-bdd8f6f370e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140363/selection/0fd1f53d810123760f0a4dea5516a22798ac28fdc9ee9b8aac95b13bef853fb1" :answer-field/choices ["q-140363/selection/eba8ed19051b1c86febb753ff1f361fda7d042ce44e03ec8c3d9a6ee23164c50" "q-140363/selection/415411ac4222f8d7004483a8d45b8894eb258ef4b817965128ee936d1f6dc577" "q-140363/selection/13a2c3dec80713ec93b0c7add6e42720c6ac44313e2be81191f977bd4ee58dfd" "q-140363/selection/0fd1f53d810123760f0a4dea5516a22798ac28fdc9ee9b8aac95b13bef853fb1" "q-140363/selection/de81b9d7ecf817e60cb92e53a68b955801e63a5b48151989590729efe8d4345c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140363" :question/id #uuid "2862936f-332b-550b-8128-3ebb5c231f35" :question/math-academy-id "q-140363" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the plane given that $v⊥w.$" :question/worked-solution "Since our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ \nAnd, since the set ${v,w}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot v}{v\\cdot v}v=\\frac{0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}v=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot w}{w\\cdot w}w=\\frac{0\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 1}{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}w=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140363/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "acb4bd03-9b89-5775-a700-e1f3ea9fa62e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140363"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140365/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "e595d57e-8f1b-5271-bc11-08cdd9d7e40f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140365/selection/edcc8b25b9f881b7ceda72d66a231a9c1e57a97ea2152d5f43bbfe8ddae028e7" :answer/id #uuid "b951abce-6f2c-5b1b-9954-3738da63d2e4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "2$\\sqrt{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140365/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "aa8bfcc2-456b-5789-b5a8-2d2cd146ed1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140365/selection/9f6bfd6fa85d96298a99db901d9b73f609ef64ac0bcf5fbdc4a7ac6d3b733558" :answer/id #uuid "0fd62cda-5f9e-59f1-a322-df83c95ecaa9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140365/selection/a6927ab90600258381c2b554f8f5f2fed3def891692738af9f06acd9bcdcbe4b" :answer/id #uuid "2de0e2af-5751-5c9e-a8a5-4b5a3756a8d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "3$\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140365/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "29bac39c-2279-56b2-8d8b-7db03c633d5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140365/selection/9f6bfd6fa85d96298a99db901d9b73f609ef64ac0bcf5fbdc4a7ac6d3b733558" :answer-field/choices ["q-140365/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-140365/selection/edcc8b25b9f881b7ceda72d66a231a9c1e57a97ea2152d5f43bbfe8ddae028e7" "q-140365/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" "q-140365/selection/9f6bfd6fa85d96298a99db901d9b73f609ef64ac0bcf5fbdc4a7ac6d3b733558" "q-140365/selection/a6927ab90600258381c2b554f8f5f2fed3def891692738af9f06acd9bcdcbe4b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140365" :question/id #uuid "b81c461c-b264-58e4-a163-7f243a57371b" :question/math-academy-id "q-140365" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ given that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{4\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0+2\\cdot (-1)}{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{(-1)}^{2}}{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{4\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\overset{^}{x}) & =‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4-3)^{2}+(0-2)^{2}+(2-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140365/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8eb07a32-45bd-5975-9f61-de6294d4895d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140365"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
